## How to validate any change
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Golden test: run a fixed range with a fixed cutoff on the old binary and the
new one and diff the sorted output. Example, for several filters:

    Immolate.exe -f erratic_flush_five -s 11111111 -n 20000000 -c 3 > old.txt
    (rebuild)
    Immolate.exe -f erratic_flush_five -s 11111111 -n 20000000 -c 3 > new.txt
    sort old.txt > old.s && sort new.txt > new.s && fc old.s new.s

The cutoff is fixed for the whole run, so the printed set is deterministic
for a given -s, -n and -c regardless of launch geometry. When comparing
against a build older than this change, note that the old binary raised its
cutoff as it went and so printed a subset of what the new one prints; compare
the old output against the new one filtered to scores >= the old maximum, or
simply confirm every seed the old build printed appears in the new output.

